<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Horus</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Horus was an ancient Egyptian sky god, shown as a falcon or a falcon-headed man. In myth he was the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osiris">Osiris</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isis">Isis</a> who avenged his father against Set, and every living king was seen as Horus on earth, using a Horus name written in a serekh. His early cult centre was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nekhen">Nekhen</a>, and he was later worshipped widely, notably at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edfu">Edfu</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/horus.jpg" alt="Horus" width="320" height="732" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jeff Dahl · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Horus_standing.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
